SYNTHETIC – 8.1 entry with a 30,000-character text data stream (a surrogate pair at
character 19,999) and long variables: a 250-character name, then 25 values of 2,500
characters (the first with a surrogate pair at character 1,999). Expected: data cut at
19,999 characters (the pair is not split), truncated, totalChars; the name cut at 200 with
nameTruncated; each value cut at 2,000 (the first at 1,999); once the 40,000-character budget
is used up, the remaining values are empty and truncated.

Frames use the fixed nonce 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; a replay replaces it with the
nonce of its request. Lines without the frame prefix are vendor noise the classifier ignores.
Used by QueueEntryV81ContractTest (tasks.md T026, research D-18, D-19).
